@startuml
title POST /api/testnet/wallet — faucet: mint and fund a throwaway test wallet
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

actor "Test author" as Author #FFD8C2
participant "TestnetApiSdk\n.getWallet()" as SDK #D5EAF7
participant "Embers API" as API #FFC9A8
participant "TestnetService" as Domain #CDEACC
participant "F1r3node chain" as Chain #FFE4A6

Author -> SDK : getWallet()
SDK -> API : POST /api/testnet/wallet
API -> Domain : create_wallet()
Domain -> Domain : generate a fresh\nsecp256k1 keypair
Domain -> Domain : render fund_test_wallet.rho\nservice wallet -> new wallet,\namount 1,000,000,000
Domain -> Chain : deploy the funding contract\n(signed by the service key)
Domain --> API : CreateTestwalletResp { key }
API --> SDK : 200 { key: hex secret key }
SDK -> SDK : PrivateKey.tryFromHex(key)
SDK --> Author : PrivateKey

note over Domain, Chain #FFF6C9
The response does not await finalization of the
funding deploy: reading the balance or spending
immediately can race the funding block.
end note

note over API #FAD8D8
Test-network convenience only. The private key
is generated server-side and transits the
network in the response: never hold real value
with a wallet minted here.
end note
@enduml
